  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday) I\nissued at 840 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nNot much change is expected in the overall weather pattern as we head\nthrough the long term period. Dangerous heat continues to be a threat\nthrough at least Sunday with Heat Risk forecast to remain at moderate\n(level 2 of 4) to major (level 3 of 4). The upper level ridge \nremains entrenched over the central and southeastern US with high \npressure dominant underneath. As a result, hot and dry conditions \ncontinue through the weekend. While we cannot rule out a low (10-20%)\nchance of an isolated thunderstorm each afternoon, confidence is \nquite low in this occurring and most locations will likely remain \ndry. Afternoon highs each afternoon will rise into the mid to upper \n90s with heat indices between 100-105F. The dome of high pressure \nbegins to recede back to the west on Monday, which will provide some \nrelief to the heat with afternoon highs only in the lower 90s. \nHowever, models continue to trend later with this occurring and it \nwill be something we will watch as we get closer in time.",
